<Defs>

  <!--
    The Ashen Banner (docs/design/peoples-next.md, the seventh of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release E";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesE2.cs): a free company that outlived its war, its king and its kingdom, and kept the
    Roll, every name lost under the banner, read aloud once a year. Neither friend nor enemy; for hire; they keep a contract
    better than most keep their word. Medieval, on the game's tribal parent, with the outlanders' stories; they arise in
    every age (ariseAges 0~3) and take the issued kit of the age they live in (ageArms: weapons and armour): spears and
    war tribalwear among the tribes, pikes, crossbows and plate in the medieval age, rifles, flak and helmets in the
    industrial age, charge rifles and recon armour in the spacer age. The clearest uniform: the company's ash-grey tabard
    (Vanilla Factions Expanded - Medieval 2) over matching issued armour dyed the same ash, the game's plate in the medieval
    age; only scars, wear and a few personal trophies tell them apart. Officers (sergeants, the captain) leave the plate for a
    cape and add a black sash (Biotech). A few are A RimWorld of Magic's commanders, gladiators and rangers. Their towns
    are barracks forts with a drill yard and the hall of the Roll (Rimfolk_Plan_BannerFort). At the gate: a squad hired for
    a season, who camp by the colony and take up arms against whatever comes, paid every five days or gone
    (Rimfolk_Evt_BannerHire); a deserter asking shelter (Rimfolk_Evt_BannerDeserter); the Roll read at the colony's gate
    for those of the colony who fell fighting (Rimfolk_Evt_BannerRoll). Their ask: a doctor for their wounded after a
    contract (Rimfolk_Mission_BannerWounded). Their founding: Corra Mallin, the quartermaster who would not let the company
    scatter unpaid. Faith (Ideology): loyalty, the company as one, and Alpha Memes' bulwark. They raid only when the colony
    has turned them hostile. Kinds of people: hussars, neanderthals, uhlans, boarskins, venators, Uredde, gorillas and
    Korgs, four in five baseliners.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="TribeBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_AshenBanner</defName>
    <label>Ashen Banner</label>
    <description>A free company for hire, neither friend nor enemy to anyone, that holds walls and fights battles for whoever pays and keeps a contract better than most people keep their word. They fought once for a king nobody remembers; the war, the king and the kingdom are gone, and the company is still here.\n\nTheir ways began the winter after that war, with the company's quartermaster, Corra Mallin, who would not let five hundred soldiers scatter unpaid into the hills. She sold every banner but one, burned grey in the last battle, and hired the company to the first town that would pay. Those who stayed with her began the Roll, the name of everyone lost under that banner, and it is read aloud once a year on the night of the last battle. A soldier of the Banner still wears its ash-grey tabard, and officers a black sash for the dead.\n\nThey are dry, plain-spoken and exact about money, and they do not boast. They will hold any wall for a season, and if the pay stops they walk. Each fort is kept by its keeper of the Roll, and the Banner by its captain.</description>
    <pawnSingular>soldier of the Banner</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>soldiers of the Banner</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>captain of the Banner</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
