    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Roll</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>A contract is kept to its last day, and the company is everyone under the banner together: what one earns all eat, and nobody is left on a field. Those who fall are not forgotten; every name is written on the Roll and read aloud on the night of the last battle, so that the company remembers what it cost. A wall held is the whole of the work. Corra Mallin sold every banner but the one that burned and kept five hundred soldiers together when the king was dead, and the first name on the Roll is the one she wrote that winter.</ideoDescription>
